# Pre-commit: format and lint what changed, and keep the types honest.
#
# Deliberately does NOT run the test suite. A pre-commit hook that takes minutes
# gets bypassed with `--no-verify`, and a bypassed hook protects nothing - which
# is worse than no hook, because it looks like a safeguard. Tests are
# `npm run verify`'s job, and that runs in CI.
#
# What IS here, and why each one:
#
#   1. lint-staged - prettier and eslint over the changed files only. Every
#      commit in this repo's history that had to be "fixed" for formatting was a
#      commit that could have been formatted on the way in, and it costs the
#      reviewer nothing to catch.
#   2. types:generate - `types/` is committed, and it is the file most likely
#      to go stale silently, because nothing about editing `src/` mentions it.
#      Regenerating and staging it here means a commit that changes a JSDoc type
#      can no longer leave the published `.d.ts` describing the old one.
npx --no-install lint-staged

# Keep `types/` in step with `src/`. Cheap, and it is the check that is easiest
# to forget - it only fails at release time, in CI, when it is most expensive.
npm run --silent types:generate

if ! git diff --quiet -- types; then
  echo "types/ was out of date; staging the regenerated declarations."
  git add types
fi
